menu "SCINTIX P4 board"

config SCINTIX_BOARD_REV_1_2
    bool "Board rev 1.2: enable USB Type-A 5V via a GPIO"
    default y
    help
        SCINTIX P4 board revision 1.2 wires an ESP32-P4 GPIO to the CM4/CM5 IO
        board's USB Type-A (host) 5V power switch. The firmware drives it high at
        boot so the USB Type-A port is powered, which is required for bus-powered
        USB peripherals such as a keyboard.

        Earlier rev 1.1 boards (same ESP32-P4 chip rev 3.1/3.2) do not connect this
        pin to the CMx expansion connector, so this can be turned off there — driving
        the GPIO on a rev 1.1 board is harmless but has no effect.

config SCINTIX_USB_A_PWR_EN_GPIO
    int "GPIO that enables the USB Type-A 5V switch"
    depends on SCINTIX_BOARD_REV_1_2
    default 23
    range 0 56
    help
        The ESP32-P4 GPIO driven high at boot to enable the CM IO board's USB
        Type-A 5V power switch. GPIO23 on SCINTIX P4 rev 1.2.

config SCINTIX_ETHERNET
    bool "On-module Ethernet (KSZ8091RNA PHY)"
    default y
    help
        Bring up the SCINTIX P4 on-module Ethernet (ESP32-P4 EMAC + Microchip
        KSZ8091RNACA PHY over RMII) with DHCP, alongside Wi-Fi. Needs a carrier
        with an RJ45, e.g. the Raspberry Pi CM4/CM5 IO board. The web settings
        page and the /agent WebSocket answer on every interface.

config SCINTIX_ETH_PHY_ADDR
    int "Ethernet PHY address"
    depends on SCINTIX_ETHERNET
    default 0
    range 0 31

config SCINTIX_ETH_PHY_RST_GPIO
    int "Ethernet PHY reset GPIO (-1 = none)"
    depends on SCINTIX_ETHERNET
    default 51
    range -1 56

endmenu
